web: gunicorn app:app --bind 0.0.0.0:${PORT:-5000}
# Example 27: Buildpack Deploy Without a Dockerfile. (co-17)
#
# A Procfile declares your process TYPES and their start commands. A buildpack
# reads it, DETECTS your language (Python, here, from requirements.txt), and
# supplies the runtime -- zero image authoring required. This is the
# "convenience" half of co-17's trade-off. Save as ./Procfile in the repo and
# `git push` (Example 26's flow); the PaaS uses it instead of a Dockerfile.

# --- Line anatomy: <type>: <command> -----------------------------------------
# web          => a PROCESS TYPE named 'web' (the PaaS routes HTTP to this type)
# gunicorn ... => the exact start command the buildpack-installed gunicorn runs
# ${PORT:-5000} => the PaaS injects $PORT at runtime; default 5000 if unset
# 0.0.0.0      => bind ALL interfaces INSIDE the container; the PaaS proxy maps it out

# (Optional) a second process type for a background worker, demonstrating that
# one push can declare MANY process types (co-16/co-17). Uncomment to use:
# worker: python worker.py

# --- Verify (after `git push`) ------------------------------------------------
#   ssh dokku@<box> ps:report myapp   # => shows the 'web' process type, running
#   curl http://<box>/<app-url>       # => the buildpack-built app answers
# [verify] a reproducible build with NO Dockerfile in the repo (co-17's buildpack half).